# Cargo / Rust
target/
# Cargo.lock is deliberately TRACKED (not ignored): this workspace builds
# native binaries and CI gates on trajectory hashes, so dependency
# resolution must be reproducible across runs. Without it, every CI run
# re-resolved ("Locking 56 packages"), which silently changed the
# dependency set under the determinism gates. Bump it deliberately in a
# dependency-update commit, and re-run the `msrv` job (a newer
# transitive release can raise the MSRV).

# .NET build outputs
bin/
obj/
artifacts/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# IDE / editor
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo

# Test results
TestResults/
*.trx

# OS / local
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local-only legacy native dir at repo root (we stage runtimes/ instead).
# Anchored with leading slash: a bare "native/" would also match
# src/PhiEng.Native/runtimes/<rid>/native/, which MUST stay tracked.
/native/

